VulkanBVH: reusable Vulkan compute acceleration structures.

Core:
  bvh/bvh.hpp             GPU LBVH with multiple independently owned trees
  bvh/hierarchy.hpp       Sharded TLAS + per-mesh BLAS, world instances
  bvh/shaders/bvh.comp    Morton, GPU radix sort, topology, refit, ray/AABB
  bvh/shaders/hierarchy.comp  Exact TLAS->BLAS ray/triangle traversal

Construction:
  30-bit Morton keys with stable, portable 4-bit LSD radix sorting.
  Eight passes of histogram, prefix and scatter (24 dispatches total).
  Karras longest-common-prefix topology with parallel AABB refit.
  update_bounds()+record_refit() skips resort and topology creation.
  Shared Vulkan pipeline layouts and shader pipelines minimize BLAS setup.
  Individual bvh::tree objects replace the old single-tree restriction;
  the free functions remain compatible wrappers around a default tree.

Two-level hierarchy:
  bvh::hierarchy stores one BLAS per unique mesh and multiple TLAS chunks
  of up to 65,536 instances. Nodes and triangles are packed on the GPU.
  A single compute shader traverses TLAS, transforms rays with user-supplied
  world-to-local matrices, and performs exact BLAS triangle intersections.
  Result includes mesh-local primitive ID, global instance ID and distance.
  Both closest-hit and any-hit traversal are supported.
  Instance count and bounds may change only by rebuilding or refitting
  with an unchanged count, respectively. Geometry may be GPU-updated
  through mesh_tree(i).triangles_descriptor()/primitives_descriptor()
  before record_refit() copies newly refitted BLAS data into the hierarchy.
  Caller owns GPU submission fences and cross-pass barriers.

Shader compilation belongs to the application build, as with render/.
  Compile bvh.comp to ten SPIR-V variants in this exact shader_paths order:
    BVH_KEYS
    BVH_CLEAR
    BVH_TOPOLOGY
    BVH_LEAVES
    BVH_REFIT
    BVH_OVERLAP
    BVH_RAY
    BVH_RADIX_HISTOGRAM
    BVH_RADIX_PREFIX
    BVH_RADIX_SCATTER
  Compile hierarchy.comp once with glslangValidator -V -S comp.
  There is no tools directory and no runtime shader compiler.

Limits:
  One BLAS <= 65,536 triangles; TLAS chunks <= 65,536 instances.
  BVH traversal stacks are fixed (64 for hierarchy, 96 for base BVH).
  An overflow flags the answer as inconclusive.
  Build/refit performance and GPU numerical correctness have not yet been
  benchmarked or hardware-tested. Moving triangles require a matching
  updated AABB per leaf, not only new vertex positions. A hierarchy is
  useful for GPU ray queries; it should not be built in an application
  that only performs ordinary rasterization without ray queries.
